  "solution": "Divide \\(x^3\\) by \\(x^2+5x+1\\):\n\n\\[\nx^3 = (x-5)(x^2+5x+1) + (24x+5)\n\\]\n\nCheck:\n\n\\[\n(x-5)(x^2+5x+1)=x^3-24x-5\n\\]\n\nso adding \\(24x+5\\) gives \\(x^3\\).\n\nSince the remainder \\(24x+5\\) has degree \\(1<2\\), it is the required remainder.\n\nThe answer is \\(24x+5\\).",
